 Hi Mariana, 



 can you please send us a link to the test issue spreadsheet? 

 We found the following issues so far: 


 When creating a trigger and selecting a specific template, a new webhook subscription is created. However the
 subscription is not subscribing to events of a specific template. Instead it is listening to hooks from all templates. If you add the template ID to the subscription URL like you can see here it will only send hooks for passes of a specific template creating
 less load and noise: 
https://developer.passcreator.com/space/API/23331116/Subscription+endpoint What endpoint are you using to pull the list of templates? In our case they are usually ordered by modified on
 in Passcreator. The order in Albato is different but we don’t really see a logic. How can existing Automations be updated? I can see I can edit the connection settings by clicking the three dots
 but what should I do if I need to e.g. change the template? Delete the Step 1 and create a new one? When pausing an Automation, Albato does not unsubscribe but when starting it again, it subscribes again.

This means that there will be multiple webhook subscriptions when pausing and restarting Automations currently. Naming issue with triggers – can you please rename them? 
 A scanning application should be “A pass was scanned (App Scan created)” The pass has been active should be “A pass was saved in Wallet” The pass has been deactivated should be “A pass was removed from Wallet or updates have been disabled” 
 Naming issue with actions: 
 Update a new pass should be “Update an existing pass” Bulk update passes (beta) should be “Bulk update passes” (we’ll remove the beta flag in a few days) Sending a push notification to the card should be “Send a push notification to a pass” Sending Push notifications in multiple passes should be “Send a push notification to multiple passes” 




